  "question": {
    "text": "An electric current is flowing through a circular coil of radius $\\mathrm{R}$. The ratio of the magnetic field at the centre of the coil and that at a distance $2 \\sqrt{2} R$ from the centre of the coil and on its axis is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$2 \\sqrt{2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n27\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n36\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n8",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $:$ Radius $=R$\nDistance $\\mathrm{x}=2 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{R}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{B_{\\text {centre }}}{B_{\\text {axis }}} & =\\left(1+\\frac{x^2}{R^2}\\right)^{3 / 2}=\\left(1+\\frac{(2 \\sqrt{2} R)^2}{R^2}\\right)^{3 / 2} \\\\\n& =(9)^{3 / 2}=27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}